  "english": "The beginning is \"God\" [Astuats]. Evening Sun-[Hymn] Tone 6 [g-k].\n\"Dead and our\" [Mreol yev mer]. Eve of the Fast of Saint James [Surb Hakob].\n\n13. Wednesday. Tone 1 [a-dz]. Fathers Tone 8 [d-k]: \"God of our fathers, have mercy.\"\n\n17. Sunday. Tone 3 [g-dz]. Fourth [Sunday]. Fathers Tone 5 [g-dz]: \"Glorified Son.\" Evening Sun-[Hymn] Tone 5 [g-dz]: \"Glorifying is Your,\" to the end.\n\n23. Saturday. Tone 2 [b-dz]. [Feast] of David the Prophet and James the Apostle.\n\n24. Sunday. Tone 4 [b-k]. Fifth [Sunday]. Fathers Tone 6 [g-k]: \"Pre-eternal.\" Evening Sun-[Hymn] Tone 4 [b-k]: \"Morning,\" to the end.\n\n29. Friday. Tone 1 [a-dz]. Eve of the Nativity Fast.\n\n30. Saturday. Tone 2 [a-k]. Fast of the Nativity of Christ. — Basil, etc.\n\n31. Sunday. Tone 2 [b-dz]. Sixth [Sunday] of the Fast. Evening Sun-[Hymn] Tone 3 [b-dz]: \"Today they rejoiced,\" to the end.\nAnd read the services in order.\n\nJanuary\n\n1. Monday. Tone 4 [b-k]. Fast. Fathers Tone 8 [d-k]: \"Blessed Lord God, blessed.\"\n\n5. Friday. Tone 8 [d-k]. Eve of the Nativity of Christ.\n\nSeven-day cycle of the Romans, 6 January.\nThursday:\n\n6. THURSDAY. Feast of the Nativity and Epiphany of Christ. The meat-eating period [between feasts] is twenty-five days.\n\n13. Thursday. Eighth day of the Nativity, and the Circumcision of Christ.\n\n15. Saturday. [Feast] of John the Forerunner [Karapet].\n\n16. Sunday. First [Sunday]. Fathers Tone 7 [d-dz]: \"Dawn of the Only-begotten.\" See in the Directory page 100, until the Eve of the Fast of Catechumens [Arachavorats], keeping the dates of the month.\n\n30. Sunday. Third [Sunday]. Eve of the Fast of Catechumens [Arachavorats]. And for the rest, see the First Volume.\n\nFebruary\n\n7. Monday. [Feast] of the Atomian Saints, — and of Bishop Mark, and of Pionius, etc.\n\n14. Monday. Presentation of the Lord [Tyarnndaraj].\n\n20. Sunday. Tone 8 [d-k]. Great Barekendan [Great Lent Eve]. See also the others according to their order in the First Volume until Vardavar, keeping the local order.\n\nApril\n\n7. Thursday. Tone 6 [g-k]. Great [Thursday]. Feast of the Annunciation of the Holy Virgin.\n\n10. Sunday. Tone 1 [a-dz]. Easter [Zatik]. Day of the Resurrection of Christ. See according to the order in the First Volume.\n\nMay\n\n19. Thursday. Tone 8 [d-k]. Ascension of Christ. See according to the order in the First Volume.\n\n29. Sunday. Tone 2 [a-k]. Coming of the Holy Spirit [Pentecost]. Eve of the Eliatic Fast.\n\nJune\n\n5. Sunday. Tone 1 [a-dz]. First [Sunday]. Beginning of the Sundays of the Resurrection. Fathers Tone 1 [a-dz]: \"Who came for the salvation of the universe.\"\n\nJuly\n\n17. Sunday. Tone 2 [b-dz]. Vardavar [Transfiguration]. The meat-eating period [between feasts] is three weeks. See in the First Volume until the Eve of the Assumption of the Mother of God, only see the order of the Fathers [hymns] here.",
